[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] # Testing Guide
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] Test files in this repository do **not** use the `.test` suffix on either the JavaScript or Rust side. JavaScript tests live next to their Rust counterparts with matching base names so the two languages stay in lockstep.
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ## Running Tests Manually
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] All tests can be executed manually using Bun's built-in test runner (JS) or `cargo test` (Rust).
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ### Prerequisites
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] Make sure dependencies are installed:
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ```bash
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] bun install
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ```
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ### Run Unit Tests (Default)
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] Unit tests run quickly without API calls. These are the tests that run with `npm test`:
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ```bash
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] cd js && npm test
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ```
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] This expands to `bun test ./tests/*.js ./tests/*.ts` and covers every JavaScript unit test under `js/tests/` (not the ones in `js/tests/integration/`).
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] > **Why explicit paths?** Bun's auto-discovery requires the `.test`, `.spec`, `_test_`, or `_spec_` suffix. Because we want the JavaScript file names to match the Rust ones (which never use `.test`), we pass explicit paths instead of relying on auto-discovery.
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ### Integration Tests
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] > **Important**: Integration tests make real API calls and should be run **one at a time** to avoid exhausting rate limits. Never run all integration tests at once.
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] Integration tests live in `js/tests/integration/`. To run a single integration test:
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ```bash
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] # Run the basic "hi" integration test (recommended default)
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] npm run test:integration
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] # Run a specific integration test
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] bun test ./js/tests/integration/basic.js
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] bun test ./js/tests/integration/bash.tools.js
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ```
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] ### Why Integration Tests Are Separate
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] The default AI model (`minimax-m2.5-free`) has strict rate limits. Running multiple integration tests in bulk will exhaust the rate limit quota, causing tests to fail or wait for hours.
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] All integration tests pass `--no-retry-on-rate-limits` to the agent CLI to fail fast instead of waiting when rate limited.
[2026-09-30T10:10:04.639Z] [STDERR] 
