[2026-09-30T10:10:07.714Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"gh api repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201 && gh api repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201/comments --paginate && gh pr view 321 --repo link-assistant/agent --json body && git fetch origin && git log -1 --format='%H %cI %s' origin/main\"","aggregated_output":"{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201\",\"id\":4742692143,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOPQG3M88AAAABGq-9Lw\",\"number\":1201,\"title\":\"MarkdownRenderable silently renders raw markup (conceal stops working) with `web-tree-sitter@>=0.26` — hardcoded `web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm` was renamed upstream\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"denghongcai\",\"id\":1433247,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMyNDc=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1433247?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/denghongcai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/denghongcai/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-06-25T09:53:21Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-26T06:24:08Z\",\"closed_at\":\"2026-06-26T06:24:08Z\",\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n`@opentui/core`'s tree-sitter worker hardcodes an import of `web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm`. In `web-tree-sitter@0.26.0` that file was **renamed** to `web-tree-sitter.wasm` (and the package `exports` no longer expose `./tree-sitter.wasm`). When the resolved `web-tree-sitter` is `>=0.26`, the tree-sitter runtime fails to initialize, so the markdown grammar never loads and **`MarkdownRenderable` renders raw markup** (`##`, `**`, `` ` `` etc. are no longer concealed/styled). The failure is effectively silent — there is only a `console` warning; rendering itself doesn't throw.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- `@opentui/core`: `0.4.1` (also reproduces on `0.4.2`; both `peerDependencies.web-tree-sitter = \\\"0.25.10\\\"`)\\n- `web-tree-sitter`: `0.26.3` (broken) vs `0.25.10` (works)\\n- Runtime: Node and Bun both affected (it's a module-resolution problem, not runtime-specific)\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`parser.worker.js` resolves the web-tree-sitter runtime wasm by name:\\n\\n```js\\n// @opentui/core/parser.worker.js\\nlet treeWasm = await resolveBundledFilePath(\\n  () => import(\\\"web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm\\\", { with: { type: \\\"wasm\\\" } }),\\n  () => import.meta.resolve(\\\"web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm\\\"),\\n  import.meta.url,\\n);\\n```\\n\\n`web-tree-sitter`'s `exports` map by version:\\n\\n| version  | wasm subpath exported            |\\n| -------- | -------------------------------- |\\n| `0.25.x` | `./tree-sitter.wasm`             |\\n| `0.26.x` | `./web-tree-sitter.wasm` (renamed) |\\n\\nSo on `0.26.x`, both the dynamic `import(...)` and `import.meta.resolve(\\\"web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm\\\")` fail with `Cannot find module 'web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm'`. The TreeSitter client init throws, the markdown grammar is never available, and conceal becomes a no-op (raw markup is shown).\\n\\nObserved warning:\\n\\n```\\nTreeSitter client initialization failed: ResolveMessage: Cannot find module 'web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm'\\n```\\n\\n## Minimal reproduction\\n\\n```ts\\nimport { createCliRenderer, MarkdownRenderable, SyntaxStyle, resolveRenderLib } from \\\"@opentui/core\\\";\\n\\nconst renderer = await createCliRenderer();\\nconst lib = resolveRenderLib();\\n\\nconst md = new MarkdownRenderable(renderer, {\\n  content: \\\"## Heading\\\\n\\\\n**bold** and `code`\\\",\\n  syntaxStyle: new SyntaxStyle(lib, lib.createSyntaxStyle()),\\n  conceal: true,\\n});\\nrenderer.root.add(md);\\n\\n// web-tree-sitter@0.25.10  -> \\\"Heading  bold and code\\\"        (markers concealed) ✅\\n// web-tree-sitter@0.26.x   -> \\\"## Heading  **bold** `code`\\\"   (raw markup)        ❌\\n```\\n\\nToggle the result by installing `web-tree-sitter@0.25.10` vs `web-tree-sitter@0.26.3`.\\n\\n## Expected vs actual\\n\\n- **Expected:** markdown markers are concealed/styled regardless of which supported `web-tree-sitter` is installed.\\n- **Actual:** with `web-tree-sitter@>=0.26`, the grammar fails to load and markup renders raw.\\n\\n## Why \\\"just pin `web-tree-sitter@0.25.10`\\\" isn't a great workaround\\n\\n`@opentui/core` declaring the peer as `0.25.10` pushes the constraint onto every consumer. Apps that also depend on `web-tree-sitter@0.26+` directly (other tree-sitter grammars, newer API) end up with a hard version conflict, and resolvers (pnpm/npm) may satisfy `@opentui/core`'s peer with the consumer's `0.26.x`, silently re-triggering this bug. There's also no public way to override the runtime wasm path: the `dataPath` option only points at the **grammar** asset directory, not the `web-tree-sitter` runtime wasm.\\n\\n## Suggested fixes (any one)\\n\\n1. **Resolve both filenames** in the worker — try `web-tree-sitter/web-tree-sitter.wasm` (0.26+) first, fall back to `web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm` (≤0.25). Smallest change, supports both majors:\\n   ```js\\n   const treeWasm = await resolveBundledFilePath(\\n     () => import(\\\"web-tree-sitter/web-tree-sitter.wasm\\\", { with: { type: \\\"wasm\\\" } })\\n            .catch(() => import(\\\"web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm\\\", { with: { type: \\\"wasm\\\" } })),\\n     () => { try { return import.meta.resolve(\\\"web-tree-sitter/web-tree-sitter.wasm\\\"); }\\n             catch { return import.meta.resolve(\\\"web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm\\\"); } },\\n     import.meta.url,\\n   );\\n   ```\\n2. **Bump the peer range** to support `web-tree-sitter@^0.26` and use the new filename.\\n3. **Expose an override** for the runtime wasm path (e.g. extend `dataPath`/a `wasmPath` option) so consumers can point at the correct file.\\n4. **Surface the init failure** (throw or a prominent error) instead of silently degrading to raw markup — this took a while to diagnose precisely because rendering \\\"works\\\" but conceal silently stops.\\n\",\"closed_by\":{\"login\":\"simonklee\",\"id\":52795,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzk1\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52795?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/simonklee\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":\"not_planned\",\"pinned_comment\":null}[{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/comments/4806912949\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201#issuecomment-4806912949\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201\",\"id\":4806912949,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDOPQG3M88AAAABHoOrtQ\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"simonklee\",\"id\":52795,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzk1\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52795?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/simonklee\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/simonklee/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-06-26T06:24:08Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-26T06:24:08Z\",\"body\":\"Thanks for the report. \\n\\n@opentui/core currently pins and supports web-tree-sitter@0.25.10 exactly. 0.26.x includes broader breaking changes beyond the renamed Wasm file, so resolving both filenames would imply support we have not established.\\n\\nPlease use web-tree-sitter@0.25.10 with current OpenTUI releases. Support for 0.26.x will be handled as a deliberate dependency upgrade with full compatibility testing rather than a local fallback. Closing as unsupported dependency configuration (for now)\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"pin\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/anomalyco/opentui/issues/comments/4806912949/reactions\",\"total_count\":1,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":1,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null}]{\"body\":\"Fixes #319.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Update all unblocked JavaScript and Rust direct dependencies to their current releases, including `ai` 7, the AI SDK providers, `command-stream` 1.3, `lino-objects-codec` 0.8, and `lino-arguments` 0.3. Refresh both JavaScript lockfiles and `Cargo.lock`.\\n- Add a daily and pull request dependency freshness workflow. It runs `npm outdated` and `cargo outdated --root-deps-only --exit-code 1`; the npm check accepts a pin only while its linked GitHub issue is open.\\n- Add a patch changeset and Rust changelog fragment so the release workflows publish the updated packages after merge. Hive Mind's Agent pin is tracked by [hive-mind#2324](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2324) R1 and can move after the npm release.\\n\\n## AI SDK 6 to 7 migration\\n\\n- Convert the local echo and cache providers from Language Model V2 to V4, including the specification version, nested token usage, structured finish reasons, and stream events. Old cached AI SDK 6 responses are normalized when read.\\n- Pass trusted system prompts through `instructions` in agent selection, generation, compaction, summaries, and titles. AI SDK 7 rejects system messages in `messages`.\\n- Replace `stepCountIs` with `isStepCount` and consume the renamed `stream` property instead of `fullStream`.\\n- Expose the synthetic echo provider for explicit `--model link-assistant/echo` runs, supply its model metadata, and select it when `--dry-run` has no explicit model.\\n\\n## Reproduction and pin exceptions\\n\\nBefore this change, `npm outdated` listed 59 stale direct declarations. The new AI SDK 7 compatibility test failed against the V2 echo/cache providers. The packed package installed with two peer warnings when the newest `solid-js` and `web-tree-sitter` were selected.\\n\\nOpenTUI 0.5.12 requires exact peer versions that are older than those packages' latest releases. `solid-js` remains at 1.9.12 until [OpenTUI #689](https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui/issues/689) is resolved. `web-tree-sitter` remains at 0.25.10 until [Agent #322](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/322) is resolved; OpenTUI confirmed that 0.26+ is currently unsupported. The pin URLs are recorded in `js/package.json` and validated by the freshness check.\\n\\nThe earlier Security run failed on the old lockfile's high severity `fast-uri` advisory ([run 36601797955](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/actions/runs/36601797955), log lines 4047–4048). The updated lockfile passes `npm audit --package-lock-only --audit-level=high`; two low severity Babel findings remain through OpenTUI.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `npm test`: 797 pass, 4 existing todo, 0 fail.\\n- `bun test ./tests/integration/dry-run.js`: 20 pass, 0 fail.\\n- `npm run check`, changeset validation, and `bun install --frozen-lockfile`: pass.\\n- Packed package installed in a fresh Bun project without peer warnings.\\n- `node ../scripts/check-npm-freshness.mjs`: pass with the two linked exceptions; `cargo outdated --root-deps-only --exit-code 1`: pass.\\n- `cargo test --all-features`, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features`: pass.\\n- `npm audit --package-lock-only --audit-level=high`: pass.\\n- Hive Mind `--tool agent` command-shape smoke: one-shot and live `stream-json` CLI runs pass with the local package and synthetic echo model; Hive Mind's own JSON stream parser confirms the echoed assistant message and successful result.\\n\\n<!-- hive-mind:changes:start -->\\n### Changes\\n- 33 file(s) modified\\n- 3566 line(s) added\\n- 5556 line(s) removed\\n- Files:\\n  - `.github/workflows/dependency-freshness.yml`\\n  - `.github/workflows/rust.yml`\\n  - `experiments/issue-319/npm-outdated-baseline.json`\\n  - `experiments/issue-319/opentui-web-tree-sitter-issue.md`\\n  - `experiments/issue-319/rust_versions.py`\\n  - `js/.changeset/dependency-refresh.md`\\n  - `js/bun.lock`\\n  - `js/experiments/issue-304-summary-rejection.mjs`\\n  - `js/experiments/model-resolved-fake-provider.mjs`\\n  - `js/package-lock.json`\\n  - `js/package.json`\\n  - `js/src/agent/agent.ts`\\n  - `js/src/cli/input-queue.js`\\n  - `js/src/cli/model-config.js`\\n  - `js/src/provider/cache.ts`\\n  - `js/src/provider/echo.ts`\\n  - `js/src/provider/opencode-zen.ts`\\n  - `js/src/provider/provider.ts`\\n  - `js/src/session/compaction.ts`\\n  - `js/src/session/processor.ts`\\n  - `js/src/session/prompt.ts`\\n  - `js/src/session/summary.ts`\\n  - `js/tests/ai-sdk-7-compat.ts`\\n  - `js/tests/ai-sdk-warnings.ts`\\n  - `js/tests/integration/dry-run.js`\\n  - `js/tests/integration/model-resolved-event.js`\\n  - `rust/Cargo.lock`\\n  - `rust/Cargo.toml`\\n  - `rust/changelog.d/20260929_172500_dependency_refresh.md`\\n  - `rust/src/id.rs`\\n  - `scripts/check-npm-freshness.mjs`\\n  - `scripts/package-info.mjs`\\n  - `scripts/use-module.mjs`\\n<!-- hive-mind:changes:end -->\\n\"}\nf681beb5c7af4f760bfafc9fd092bd2625715d9b 2026-09-29T18:33:46+00:00 0.26.8\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
