[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +# Agent #322: prepare the bash parser while OpenTUI remains blocked
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +Checked on 2026-09-30. This work addresses Agent's parser migration; it does not
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +complete [Agent #322](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/322).
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +## Upstream blocker
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +The latest `@opentui/core` and `@opentui/solid` releases are 0.5.13. Core still
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +declares `web-tree-sitter: "0.25.10"` as an exact peer and its published worker
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +still resolves `web-tree-sitter/tree-sitter.wasm`. The latest `web-tree-sitter`,
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +0.27.0, exports `web-tree-sitter/web-tree-sitter.wasm` instead.
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +The [upstream maintainer's response](https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui/issues/1201#issuecomment-4806912949)
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +confirms that 0.26+ has additional breaking changes and is unsupported. The
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +[proposed filename fallback](https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui/pull/1203)
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +was closed without merging. Changing only Agent's WASM path cannot fix OpenTUI's
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +worker or peer contract. Keep the exact 0.25.10 dependency and the open #322 URL
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +in `dependencyPins`; #322 must stay open until a compatible upstream release
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +passes the full acceptance criteria.
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +Check the published metadata again with:
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +```sh
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +npm view @opentui/core version peerDependencies --json --prefer-online
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +npm view @opentui/solid version peerDependencies --json --prefer-online
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +npm view web-tree-sitter version exports --json --prefer-online
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +```
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +## Reproduction and regression coverage
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +From the repository root:
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +```sh
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +bun experiments/issue-322/verify-bash-parser.mjs
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +```
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +The script packs the current source into temporary packages with 0.25.10 and
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +0.27.0, installs each in a fresh Bun project, checks its peers with `npm ls`, and
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +runs `js/tests/tool_bash.js` against the installed package. Only the temporary
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +package's `web-tree-sitter` declaration changes. It leaves the repository's pin
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +and lockfiles untouched and removes the temporary projects on exit. The same
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +script runs in the Ubuntu unit test job.
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +Before the parser change, the three functional tests passed with 0.25.10 and
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +failed with 0.27.0 because the old WASM export could not be resolved. After the
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +change, both versions initialize and execute the allowed command. Both versions
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +also reject a denied command in a shell chain and in a command substitution
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +before creating the target file. No AI credentials or network model calls are
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +needed; package installation requires registry access.
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +The production 0.25.10 package installs without incorrect-peer warnings and
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +`npm ls web-tree-sitter --all` succeeds. The experimental 0.27.0 package still
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +warns about the OpenTUI peer and `npm ls` reports `ELSPROBLEMS`. Those failures are
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +expected evidence of the remaining blocker, not a claim of OpenTUI compatibility.
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +## Remaining acceptance criteria
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +1. Upgrade to an OpenTUI release that explicitly supports the current parser
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +   runtime and verify its worker initializes and renders highlighted content.
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +2. Upgrade Agent's direct dependency and refresh both lockfiles; remove the
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +   freshness exception only once the upgrade is valid.
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +3. Rerun the bash tool tests and install the production packed package in a fresh
[2026-09-30T10:19:10.438Z] [STDERR] +   Bun project without any peer warnings or `npm ls` errors.
